# Git commits (BeTaxed)

**Every time** a commit would be appropriate — whether the user asked you to commit or not — you must **show the complete proposed commit message in the chat first**: full **subject** and full **body**, in a **single fenced or plain block**. No shorthand.

When the user **explicitly** asked you to commit: still output that **same full message in full in chat** immediately before any `git commit`.

## No surprise commits

1. **Never run `git commit` (or `git commit --amend`) unless the user explicitly asks you to commit.** Staging (`git add`) is also off-limits unless they ask for it as part of an agreed commit flow.
2. If work is done but the user did **not** ask to commit, end with a **short summary**, **`git add` paths**, and the **full proposed commit message**.

Never commit `.KB/Samples/` or `.env`. See `KB/GIT_STRATEGY.md`.
